  "subtitle": "Read the boxer in front",
  "summary": "Super Punch-Out!! is Nintendo’s Super Nintendo boxing game, viewed from behind a translucent player character. The opponent fills the space ahead, making every shift of guard or preparation for a punch easy to study. The player works toward the World Video Boxing Association championship through a cast of exaggerated fighters. A bout must be won within three minutes, turning observation into an urgent task. The challenge is to recognise an opponent’s habits, defend against the next attack and find the opening that follows.",
  "body": [
    "Super Punch-Out!! is Nintendo’s Super Nintendo boxing game, viewed from behind a translucent player character. The opponent fills the space ahead, making every shift of guard or preparation for a punch easy to study. The player works toward the World Video Boxing Association championship through a cast of exaggerated fighters. A bout must be won within three minutes, turning observation into an urgent task. The challenge is to recognise an opponent’s habits, defend against the next attack and find the opening that follows.",
    "Jabs and body blows can be aimed from either hand, while blocks, dodges and ducks provide different ways to avoid an incoming strike. An opponent’s raised gloves identify where a punch is likely to be stopped, so aiming and timing matter together. Repeatedly attacking the same defended area wastes an opportunity and invites retaliation. The view makes the exchange almost a conversation of gestures: a movement offers a clue, the player chooses a response, and a successful answer creates room for the next punch.",
    "An opponent who first seems overwhelming becomes more manageable once the player recognises the order and timing of the attacks. That makes another attempt useful even after the general controls are familiar. The three-minute limit encourages a sharper performance, with fewer wasted punches and quicker use of an exposed guard. Super Punch-Out!! carries the series’ arcade emphasis on recognisable personalities and precise responses onto the Super Nintendo, using detailed animation and the transparent viewpoint to keep the information for each exchange directly in front of the player."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Read the boxer in front",
    "A gap in the guard",
    "Winning is only the beginning"
  ],
